WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.180
Good morning, Hank. It's Tuesday, January 27th.

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:05.260
I'm in the fifth week of my office reorganization project

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.640
and as you can see it's going swimmingly.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.780
Hank, today's video comes to you in two very special parts.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.160
Part One: The Best New Years Resolution Ever

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.840
Happy New Year! Streamers!

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.720
Hank, "The Best New Years Resolution Ever: Happy New Year Streamers"

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.080
is a book that I wrote when I was a child that I have discovered during my office reorganization project.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:25.860
Three years ago on New Years Day, everybody in my family had to make one New Years resolution.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:27.480
I hated that.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.960
"Mom, why us?"
"Because."

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.900
Hank if we can take just one second away from this story,

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.540
I'd like to explore the whole question of this staircase to nowhere.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.240
When I was a kid growing up in Orlando, Florida,

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:42.960
I believed that the definition of "rich" was that you had stairs in your house.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.580
Like I believed in the whole direct relationship between richness and stairs so completely

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.260
that I thought that the IRS, like, came to your house every year and was like, "How many stairs you got?"

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:54.660
and you were like, "Thirteen." And they were like, "That'll be $20,000."

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.740
Alright, back to the story now.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:01.360
My mother promised to clean out the drawers. She hasn't done that since we left Michigan in 26!

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.700
"Mom, there is little brown things!"

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.760
Dad promised to weigh under 600 pounds. That would be a miracle...

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.720
"I promise to weigh under 600 pounds."
"But Dad, that's what you promised last year!"

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:17.080
By the way, note that you can tell Dad is fat due to his belly.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:20.960
My brother promised to take a bath. He smells like a skunk.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.760
At the bottom of the stairs, like a typical poor kid, Hank's like, "I'll take a bath!"

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:29.660
And then at the top of the stairs, little Mr. Rich Pants says, "You've never done that."

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:33.040
And me, well, I promised to try my hardest.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.240
"Bravo!!"
"Thank you."

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:39.580
And out of all the resolutions, mine was the only one to come true.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:43.720
"Yay!" And then you can see the stairs that lead up to the top of the podium.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.820
What has the first podium slot? Oh, it's "me."

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:46.740
The end.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:49.620
Oh my God, I'm so sorry. I mean Dad, you're not fat.

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.580
Mom, there is no little brown things in the cabinets.

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:56.400
And Hank, you don't sm... well, actually you could stand to take more showers.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.540
Part two: the reinvigoration of the Ning.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:00.920
Hank, the Ning has been suffering from a little bit of neglect

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:04.480
so much so that in fact many people watching this video are probably saying, "What's the Ning?"

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:05.580
Link in the sidebar.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:09.380
And I think I've come to the conclusion that we just can't run the Ning by ourselves.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.100
Hank, what we need is some Ning-masters.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.000
Ning-master's a fun word to say.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.400
It's like all the best parts of a ringmaster except you don't have to get eaten by lions.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.800
So Nerdfighters starting soon there will be a few Ning-masters

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:22.860
They're gonna feature new content on the main page of the Ning.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:25.860
They're gonna organize and moderate the crazy Ning forums.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.180
And they're generally just going to raise up the awesome levels of the Ning.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:32.980
If you are a committed made of awesome Nerdfighter who would like to be a Ning-master,

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:36.920
apply by creating a blog post telling me why you should be a Ning-master

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.960
and then I will pick a few of my favorites

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.200
and those people will become Ning-masters.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.360
Also, even if you do not want to be a Ning-master,

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:49.420
if you do want to share your creative awesome with other people on the Ning, start making blog posts.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.380
In fact even if you're uploading photos and videos, try to upload them as blog posts

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:56.400
because that makes it much more likely that we can feature them on the front page.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.300
Okay, I gotta go back to writing the Paper Towns screenplay.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.515
Hank, thanks for being awesome. Nerdfighters, oh my gosh you're so great.

